




=================

DRF : Django Rest Framework

=================


REST : represent state transfer

- GET : read data
- POST : create data
- PUT : update data
- PATCH : partial update data
- DELETE : delete data
- OPTIONS : describe the communication options for the target resource


- HEAD : same as GET but without response body
- TRACE : perform a message loop-back test along the path to the target resource
- CONNECT : establish a tunnel to the server identified by the target resource
- WebDAV : extension of HTTP/1.1 for collaborative authoring on the web
- CRUD : create, read, update, delete
- Idempotent : an operation that can be applied multiple times without changing the result beyond the initial application
- Stateless : each request from client to server must contain all the information needed to understand and process the request
- HATEOAS : Hypermedia As The Engine Of Application State
- API : Application Programming Interface
- SDK : Software Development Kit
- WSGI : Web Server Gateway Interface
- ASGI : Asynchronous Server Gateway Interface
- JSON : JavaScript Object Notation
- XML : eXtensible Markup Language
- YAML : YAML Ain't Markup Language
- OAuth : Open Authorization
- JWT : JSON Web Token
- CORS : Cross-Origin Resource Sharing
- API Gateway : a server that acts as an API front-end, receiving API requests, enforcing


